      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LEWIE KELLY (4) was a class above his rivals in his qualifier, talking advantage of the ace draw to lead before cruising home by close to 31m. Draws a couple of spots wider but has gate speed so can go forward again. Only needs to hold that form and he'll be very hard to catch. LEXY (12) has come from back row draws for close seconds in his last two starts, the latest at this circuit and distance when he raced three wide without cover but fought well to go under by a head. Cops another tough barrier but he is going well. YA RACIN CARL (10) took his strike rate at this circuit and distance to 50 per cent when he led from a similar draw and dug deep to beat LEXY last time. Can be prominent again. COWBOY CULTURE (8) was no match for LEWIE KELLY last start but he drew deep and raced wide before boxing on for second. Draws a little lower so he could get into the finish. THE WICKED WARRIOR (2) placed after racing wide last start. Could be competitive from the low draw.",
